    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🏛️</span> The Federal Reserve</h3>
        <p>The central bank, in charge of monetary policy, and the only place new PAT is made: every mint follows a written
          rule and is on the public record. It keeps itself between a floor and a ceiling (<a href="#fed-band">the Fed
          band</a>): below the floor it mints back up, a little each day; above the ceiling the excess is burned. It never
          pays a wallet. Its job is to keep the protocol stocked with PAT: it tops the <a href="#incentives">incentive budget</a> up
          every Monday, lends the House, the Bank and the Market maker the gap the moment one runs short (flash liquidity),
          and can grant PAT to a pool. It collects fines, the bounty fee and the shop fee, plus half of the protocol's weekly
          profit while it's below its ceiling. Nobody robs it: the bank heist cracks Fort Knox. <code>!reserve</code> shows
          its balance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🎁</span> The incentive budget</h3>
        <p>Pays every reward in the game: welcome PAT, level-ups, achievements, room games, pad royalties, launch grants and
          the heist vaults' floors. Each kind has a weekly allowance, and the Fed guarantees the weekly total
          (<%= sh(V3.target) %> PAT). Rewards are never printed straight into wallets. <a href="#incentives">More below</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🎰</span> The House (casino jackpot)</h3>
        <p>The casino's bankroll. Wheel spins, losing bets, rake, the bingo cut, the wager fee and 60% of every lotto ticket
          go in; it pays the wheel, blackjack wins and the fixed lotto prizes. If a big win ever runs it short, the Fed lends
          it the gap on the spot. Its profit is settled every Monday. <code>!jackpot</code> (or <code>!vault</code>) shows
          what's in it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🎟️</span> The Lotto pot</h3>
        <p>A separate rolling jackpot fed by 40% of every lotto ticket. Only a lotto jackpot win is paid from it,
          so a big lotto winner never drains the House. Capped at 100M.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🏦</span> The Bank &amp; 📈 Market maker</h3>
        <p>Two working vaults: the Bank lends PAT to players through Reserve loans and keeps the interest, and the Market
          maker puts up the starting PAT for every prediction market and keeps its trading fees. Together with the House
          they're the <a href="#protocol">capital vaults</a> you can stake in, and the Fed backs all three with flash
          liquidity.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🥷</span> Fort Knox &amp; the Casino vault</h3>
        <p>The heist vaults. Fort Knox (the bank job) collects half of what's spent in rooms, Prime Time, Season Passes,
          sticker packs and bank and store heist buy-ins; the Casino vault collects casino heist buy-ins. The incentive budget
          keeps each at 2M or more, and above its cap (<%= sh(V3.fk) %> and <%= sh(V3.cv) %>, 60% and 40% of the weekly
          budget) the extra flows back to the incentive budget. Heists pay out of them like a dividend, and the admins can
          switch that faucet on and off.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🧭</span> The routing table</h3>
        <p>Every fee in the game has a row in one table that says where it goes. A fee goes to whoever put up the PAT for the activity:
          casino play and the wager fee to the House, market and pool fees to the Market maker, loan interest to the Bank.
          Fines, the bounty fee and the shop fee go to the Federal Reserve, and spending in a room is split between Fort Knox
          and that pad's vault. The admins tune the splits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🚀</span> Boosts &amp; stage slots</h3>
        <p>The front page shows the liveliest pad: you can't buy it. Anyone can <b>boost</b> a pad with PAT to push it up
          the ranking (boosts fade by half every hour and only count while the pad is active). Stage slots are free unless
          the pad's owner sets a price. Boosts and slot fees go <b>half to that pad's vault</b> and <b>half to Fort
          Knox</b>; each pad vault pays the pad's owner, its streamers and its regulars a little every day through the
          <a href="#recipe">payout recipe</a>. An owner paying in their
          own pad sends it all to Fort Knox. Boost from the 🚀 button on a pad's page, or type <code>!boost 5000</code> in its
          chat room.</p>
        <p><b>✨ Pad cosmetics</b> (frames, name glows, badges, an animated avatar) take the same route: a pad's owner buying for
          their own pad sends 100% to Fort Knox; a gift from anyone else goes half to Fort Knox, half to that pad's vault.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🔒</span> Escrow</h3>
        <p>When you stake PAT on something that takes days (a wager, a market, a loan, a bounty, a bingo card) it leaves
          your wallet straight away and is held in escrow. Every step is recorded, so if Pepe restarts mid-game your
          PAT is either paid out or refunded: never lost, never paid twice.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2a-1. Room vaults (economy v2 E-3): only while they're live -->
  <% const _rv = (typeof roomVaults !== 'undefined') ? roomVaults : null;
     const _rf = (x) => Math.round(Number(x) || 0).toLocaleString('en-US'); %>
  <% if (_rv) { %>
  <section id="roomvaults">
    <div class="ds-eyebrow ac">REVENUE FOLLOWS THE ROOM</div>
    <h2 class="ds-h2"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">💰</span> Pad vaults</h2>
    <% const _rc = _rv.recipe || {}; const _rcc = _rc.cfg || {}; const _p = (k, d) => Math.round(100 * (_rcc[k] != null ? Number(_rcc[k]) : d)); %>
    <p class="lead">Every pad with a connected chat room has its own <b>pad vault</b>: a pool of PAT (points, not money) that belongs to the
      pad. Half of what's spent in a pad (paid commands, songs, voices, heist gear, boosts, stage slots, pad cosmetic gifts)
      goes to that pad's vault and half to Fort Knox<% if (!_rc.frozen) { %>; on commands in a pad with an owner, the
      owner's 10% royalty comes first until room payouts replace it<% } %>. Spending with no room goes all to Fort Knox, and
      so does the pad owner's (or the controlling gang's) spending in their own room. A vault holds at most
      <%= _rf(_rv.cap) %> PAT; anything above goes to Fort Knox. Anyone can add to a vault with
      <code>!padvault deposit &lt;amount&gt;</code> or the <b>Donate</b> button on the pad's About tab (deposits and donations
      never count as the pad's income).</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card wide">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">📊</span> Pad vaults now: <%= _rf(_rv.total) %> PAT</h3>
        <% if (_rv.rooms.length) { %>
        <ul>
          <% _rv.rooms.forEach((r) => { %>
            <li><% if (r.slug) { %><a href="/p/<%= encodeURIComponent(r.slug) %>?tab=about#vault"><%= r.title %></a><% } else { %><%= r.title %><% } %>:
              <b><%= _rf(r.balance) %></b> PAT (<%= _rf(r.inflow7) %> in over the last 7 days)</li>
          <% }) %>
        </ul>
        <% } else { %><p>Nothing in them yet.</p><% } %>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!padvault</code> · <code>!padvault history</code> · <code>!padvault all</code></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card wide" id="recipe">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">💸</span> The payout recipe<% if (!_rc.on) { %> <span class="new">SOON</span><% } %></h3>
        <p>Once a day each vault sets a budget: the owner's payout rate (2-15%, 10% by default) of its balance. The budget is
          split into fixed slices, and <b>each slice pays only what the room really earned</b>; the rest stays in the vault
          for a busier day:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Owner <%= _p('owner_pct', 0.15) %>%</b>: the pad's owner, when they were in the room on 3 of the last 7 days
            and the room was active on 3 of them. Capped at <%= _p('cap_i7', 0.25) %>% of the room's average daily income,
            so deposits and the owner's own spending never raise it. House pads never pay an owner.</li>
          <li><b>Gang <%= _p('gang_pct', 0.15) %>%</b>: the gang that controls the room, when it paid its upkeep (same cap).</li>
          <li><b>Streamers <%= _p('streamer_pct', 0.25) %>%</b>: by verified watch-minutes on the pad's stage (signed-in
            viewers, the page visible and playing, one session per account, up to 2 hours per viewer per streamer a day).
            Full at 600 watch-minutes a day; one streamer gets at most 60% of the slice.</li>
          <li><b>Regulars <%= _p('people_pct', 0.35) %>%</b>: people with 10+ real chat lines or 5+ minutes of speech on the
            mic that day (repeats, commands and silent mics don't count) and a PATV account at least a week old. Full at 20
            people; one person gets at most 10% of the slice.</li>
          <li><b>Room games <%= _p('games_pct', 0.10) %>%</b>: the day's prize pool for the room's raffle, top mic of the hour
            and pictionary. When it's used up the games run for XP only.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Payouts of <%= _rf(_rcc.convoy_min || 25000) %> PAT or more leave on a 10-minute convoy that people in the room can
          try to hit (a hit takes at most 20%). <code>!padvault recipe</code> shows the pad's last payout day.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>
  <% } %>

  <!-- 2a0. Incentive budget + weekly surplus waterfall (economy v2 E-2): explained only while it's live -->
  <%
    const _tr = (typeof treasury !== 'undefined') ? treasury : null;
    const _f = (x) => Math.round(Number(x) || 0).toLocaleString('en-US');
  %>
  <section id="incentives">
    <div class="ds-eyebrow ac">REWARDS HAVE A BUDGET</div>
    <h2 class="ds-h2"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🎁</span> The incentive budget</h2>
    <% if (!_tr) { %>
      <p class="lead">Coming soon: rewards (level-ups, welcome PAT, achievements, connect bonuses) will be paid from an
        <b>incentive budget</b> that the protocol fills every week out of its real profit, instead of from the Federal
        Reserve. <span class="cfg">Not switched on yet: rewards are still paid the way they are today.</span></p>
    <% } else { %>
      <p class="lead">Rewards aren't printed. Every reward in the game is paid from one budget, and each kind of reward has a
        weekly allowance. The budget is refilled every Monday from the protocol's real profit, and the Federal Reserve
        guarantees the rest of the week's total (<%= sh(V3.target) %> PAT). If an allowance runs out, your reward
        <b>waits in line</b> (first come, first paid) and lands in your wallet as soon as it refills. Nothing is ever skipped.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">📅</span> The weekly settlement</h3>
          <p>Every Monday at 04:00 UTC the House, the Bank and the Market maker each keep a target bankroll (House 15M,
            Bank 2M or twice its busiest lending, Market maker 1M or 1.5× its market seeds). The protocol's profit above
            that target is the <b>surplus</b>, and it is split in this order:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>first it repays anything that vault borrowed from the Federal Reserve;</li>
            <li><b>20%</b> to stakers in that vault, pro rata, capped at <b>25% APR</b> on what they staked (anything over
              the cap rejoins the rest);</li>
            <li>the rest: while the Federal Reserve is below its <a href="#fed-band">ceiling</a>, half to the Reserve and half to the
              incentive budget; once it's at the ceiling, <b>all of it</b> to the incentive budget.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🛟</span> The weekly guarantee</h3>
          <p>Right after the settlement, the Federal Reserve tops the incentive budget up to the week's target:
            <b><%= sh(V3.target) %> PAT</b>. A quiet week at the casino never means smaller rewards, and a busy one refills the
            Reserve instead of piling up in the budget.</p>
          <p><span class="new">SOON</span> The target will grow and shrink with how many real, verified people are active, so
            rewards follow the people who show up. Activity checks keep alts and spam out of the count.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🧮</span> What the budget pays</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><b>Heist vault floors.</b> Fort Knox and the Casino vault are topped back up to 2M each day, so heists always
              have something to rob. Above their caps (<%= sh(V3.fk) %> and <%= sh(V3.cv) %>, 60% and 40% of the weekly
              budget) the extra flows back here.</li>
            <li><b>Rewards.</b> Welcome PAT, level-ups, achievements, connect bonuses, codes and platform rewards, and pad owner
              royalties until room payouts replace them, each within its weekly allowance. Rewards over it wait in line.</li>
            <li><b>Room games.</b> The chat raffle, top mic of the hour, pictionary and !beg, paced through the week (at most
              1/7 of the allowance a day). A prize over the allowance is skipped. Once room payouts are on, a room with a vault
              pays its games from its own vault's daily slice instead.</li>
            <li><b>Turf Wars:</b> the turf income and the season prize of the current season.</li>
            <li><% if (!LP_ON) { %><span class="new">SOON</span> <% } %><b>Launch grants</b> that seed the vaults of new pads, as they build a following.</li>
            <li><span class="new">SOON</span> <b>Activity rewards</b> for people who chat and get on the mic, and <b>pad
              top-ups</b> that match what each pad vault pays out.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">📊</span> This week</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Incentive budget: <b><%= _f(_tr.balance) %> PAT</b></li>
            <% if (_tr.share !== null && _tr.share !== undefined) { %><li>From this week's settlement: <%= _f(_tr.share) %> PAT (about <%= _f(_tr.release_per_day) %> a day)</li><% } %>
            <% Object.keys(_tr.budgets || {}).forEach((g) => { %>
              <li><%- GROUP[g] || t.esc(g) %>:
                <%= _f((_tr.remaining || {})[g]) %> of <%= _f(_tr.budgets[g]) %> left</li>
            <% }) %>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% } %>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2a. Burned (1.99dk) -->
  <section id="burned">
    <div class="ds-eyebrow ac">OUT OF CIRCULATION</div>
    <h2 class="ds-h2"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🔥</span> Burned</h2>
    <p class="lead">PAT is burned in one place only: when the Federal Reserve holds more than its
      <a href="#fed-band">ceiling</a>, the daily tick releases the excess to the burn reserve and destroys it, so the total
      supply goes down. No wallet, stash, vault or game pool is ever burned. Every burn is listed here.</p>
    <div class="grid" id="burnStats" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="card"><h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🔥</span> Total burned</h3><p class="n" data-b="total">…</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Last 7 days</h3><p class="n" data-b="d7">…</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Last 30 days</h3><p class="n" data-b="d30">…</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ds-tbl"><table aria-label="Burn log">
      <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>PAT</th><th>From</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="burnLog"><tr><td colspan="4">Loading…</td></tr></tbody>
    </table></div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>
  <script src="/public/js/burns.js?v=1" defer></script>

  <!-- 2b. Protocol -->
