    <h3 class="h3s"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🏗️</span> Capital vaults: PAT that does a job</h3>
    <p class="lead">Three of those pools are <b>capital vaults</b>. Each one holds PAT that does a real job in the game and
      earns from that job. You can put your own PAT in alongside it (that's staking) and earn or lose with it.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🏦</span> Bank</h3>
        <p>Lends the PAT for Reserve loans to players (<code>!loan reserve</code>). Earns their interest and late penalties, plus the
          protocol's 10% cut of interest on loans between players.</p>
        <p><b>Risk:</b> borrowers who don't pay. A loan 30 days late is a default: the protocol's own profit in the Bank
          absorbs it first, and if that isn't enough the Federal Reserve lends the Bank the rest. The Bank keeps the claim on
          the borrower, and stakers' share price is untouched unless a default is bigger than all of that.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🎰</span> House</h3>
        <p>This <i>is</i> the casino bankroll: the jackpot that pays out wins. Earns the house edge: losing blackjack bets,
          hold'em rake, wheel spins, the lotto's margin, the bingo house cut and the 5% wager fee.</p>
        <p><b>Risk:</b> big wins, like a wheel jackpot or a blackjack streak. If a payout ever runs it short, the Federal
          Reserve lends it the gap on the spot (flash liquidity). Casino heists don't touch it: they rob the separate Casino
          vault, which the incentive budget keeps topped up. Still the most up-and-down vault.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">📈</span> Market maker</h3>
        <p>Puts up the starting PAT (the "seed") for every new prediction market, then takes that market's 2% trading fees
          and whatever's left when it settles. The fee on betting pools goes to it too.</p>
        <p><b>Risk:</b> a market can lose at most its seed.</p>
        <p>Its value counts each open market at what it expects back when it settles (the pot minus the winning
          shares, weighted by the market's own odds), not at the seed, so a one-sided market shows its coming loss
          straight away instead of at settlement.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🤖</span> Auto <span class="new">DEFAULT</span></h3>
        <p>A fund that holds all three for you, inside admin limits: <b>at least 40% Bank</b>, <b>at most 35% House</b>,
          <b>at most 25% Market maker</b>. Every day it leans toward whichever vault has done best over the last 30 days
          for the risk it took.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="note"><b>You only earn from what you fund.</b> The protocol's own PAT sits in each vault right next to
      stakers' PAT, so everyone (the protocol included) earns and loses in proportion to what they put in.</div>

