    <h3 class="h3s"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">📊</span> Shares: how a stake grows</h3>
    <p class="lead">Staking buys <b>shares</b> of a vault at today's share price (the vault's value ÷ the number of shares).
      When the vault earns, the share price goes up; when it pays out a big loss, the price goes down.
      Nothing is "paid out" to you and nothing piles up in a separate pool: your earnings compound automatically inside the price.
      Your stake is worth <b>your shares × today's price</b>, and your wallet shows that value and your profit or loss.</p>
