    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🕛</span> The daily cut-off</h3>
        <p>Stake and unstake requests don't happen instantly. They queue up and all run once a day (around midnight ET)
          at that day's price. That way nobody can jump in just before a lotto draw and jump out right after.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">💸</span> Getting your PAT out</h3>
        <p>A withdrawal needs free PAT in that vault: the Bank's PAT may be lent out, and the House always keeps a minimum float
          to pay winners. If there isn't enough, your request waits in the queue and fills as PAT frees up.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">📏</span> Limits</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Stakers can own at most <b>50%</b> of any vault, so the protocol always keeps skin in the game.</li>
          <li><b>The weekly settlement:</b> every Monday a vault's profit above its target size (the House: 15M; the Bank: 2M or twice its busiest lending; the Market maker: 1M or 1.5× its market seeds) is shared out. It first repays any Fed loan, then stakers get <b>20%</b>, and the rest goes half to the Federal Reserve (while it's below its ceiling) and half to the <a href="#incentives">incentive budget</a>. Stakers' shares are never touched.</li>
          <li><b>Ceiling:</b> stakers' share of a week is capped at 25% a year <span class="cfg">⚙</span>; anything above it rejoins the rest of the surplus.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="h3s"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">⚖️</span> Fees follow risk</h3>
    <p class="lead">A fee goes to whoever put up the PAT for that activity. Market and pool fees go to the Market maker
      that seeds the markets, loan interest goes to the Bank that lent it, casino margins and the wager fee go to the House.
      Fines, the bounty fee and the shop fee go to the Federal Reserve, and spending in a room is split between Fort Knox and
      that pad's vault, by the routing table. Stakers don't get paid for activity they don't fund.</p>

    <h3 class="h3s"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🎟️</span> The Lotto pot</h3>
    <p class="lead">Each 1,000 PAT lotto ticket splits in two: <b>40%</b> builds the Lotto pot, a separate rolling jackpot that only
      the lotto jackpot is paid from (so a jackpot win never drains the House), and <b>60%</b> goes to the House, which pays
      the smaller fixed prizes and keeps the margin. The jackpot is capped at 100M.</p>

    <h3 class="h3s"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🤔</span> Which vault is right for me?</h3>
    <div class="ds-tbl">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>VAULT</th><th>FEELS LIKE</th><th>PICK IT IF</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>🏦 Bank</td><td>Steady and insured</td><td>You want slow, reliable growth</td></tr>
          <tr><td>🎰 House</td><td>Up and down, highest on average</td><td>You can ride out a big jackpot hit</td></tr>
          <tr><td>📈 Market maker</td><td>Depends on the markets</td><td>The room is busy trading markets</td></tr>
          <tr><td>🤖 Auto</td><td>A bit of everything</td><td>You're not sure (it's the default)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="cmd"><code>!stash stake savings 100k</code> (Auto) · <code>!stash stake savings all house</code> ·
      <code>!stash unstake savings 50k bank</code> · <code>!vaults</code> or <code>!stash yield</code> for the numbers ·
      live dashboard on <a href="/staking">/staking</a></div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Casino -->
