  <!-- 8. Loans -->
  <section id="loans">
    <div class="ds-eyebrow ac">CREDIT</div>
    <h2 class="ds-h2"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🏦</span> Loans</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🤝</span> Person to person</h3>
        <p>Lend PAT with interest (a flat rate for the term, max 50%). The amount is held from you right away; they have
          10 minutes to accept. Borrowers can repay early, in part or in full.</p>
        <p>When it's due, Pepe collects automatically: whatever they have, then the rest as PAT comes in. Anything still
          owed grows 2% a day (capped at +50% of the loan) and the borrower carries a public <b>LATE</b> mark until square.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!loan @bob 50k 10% 7d</code> · <code>!loan repay L5</code> · <code>!loan check @bob</code> · <code>!loans</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> the lender always gets the full amount back; 10% of the interest and penalties goes to the Bank.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🏛️</span> Federal Reserve loans <span class="new">NEW</span></h3>
        <p>Borrow at the Reserve's rate, with the PAT lent out of the Bank vault. Within your limit it's approved instantly; your limit grows
          with your level and a clean repayment record. Want more? Ask the admins, who can also grant loans themselves.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!loan reserve 50k 7d</code> · <code>!loan request 200k 14d why</code> (bigger amounts) · <code>!loan reserve</code> shows your limit</div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> these loans are lent out of the <a href="#protocol">Bank vault</a>, so principal, interest and
          late penalties go back to the Bank (and its stakers). Unpaid loans are collected automatically, and a late borrower is
          marked LATE and can't borrow again until they're square. A loan 30 days late is a default: the Bank's own profit covers
          it first, the Federal Reserve lends the Bank anything more, and the Bank keeps collecting from the borrower.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 9. Stashes & staking -->
  <section id="stash">
    <div class="ds-eyebrow ac">SAVE &amp; EARN</div>
    <h2 class="ds-h2"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🔐</span> Stashes &amp; staking</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🔐</span> Stashes</h3>
        <p>Personal vaults. Park PAT outside your wallet and share it with accounts you trust: anyone you grant can
          deposit and withdraw. Up to 3 stashes, 10 members each. Closing one pays what's left to the owner.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!stash create savings</code> · <code>!stash deposit savings 50k</code><br><code>!stash grant savings @myalt</code> · <code>!stash withdraw savings 10k</code> · <code>!stash list</code></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">📈</span> Staking: capital vaults <span class="new">NEW</span></h3>
        <p>Stake PAT from a stash into a <a href="#protocol">capital vault</a>: the 🏦 Bank (lends PAT, insured),
          the 🎰 House (the casino bankroll, most volatile), the 📈 Market maker (seeds prediction markets), or 🤖 Auto
          (the default, a mix of all three). You buy shares; as the vault earns, the share price rises and your earnings
          compound inside it. If the vault takes a loss, the price drops.</p>
        <p>Requests run once a day at the cut-off (around midnight ET) at that day's price, and unstaking pays out
          once the vault has free PAT. Your stake goes back into the same stash.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!stash stake &lt;stash&gt; &lt;amount|all&gt; [bank|house|mm|auto]</code><br>
          <code>!stash unstake &lt;stash&gt; &lt;amount|all&gt; [vault]</code> · <code>!stash yield</code> · <code>!vaults</code></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">👛</span> Your wallet &amp; the vaults</h3>
        <p>See your stashes, stakes (value and profit or loss) and loans in one place on <a href="/wallet">/wallet</a>.
          <a href="/staking">/staking</a> is the live vault dashboard: share prices, APR, revenue by source and your positions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 10. GTF -->
  <section id="gtf">
    <div class="ds-eyebrow ac">CRIME PAYS</div>
    <h2 class="ds-h2"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🔫</span> Grand Theft Frogger</h2>
    <p class="lead">The crime side of PATV. Roll a character with <code>!sheet</code> and go to work. Full guide on <a href="/gtf">/gtf</a>.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🥷</span> Heists</h3>
        <p>Crew up and survive rounds of dice rolls to bank loot; bail out or go for the vault door. The store is always open;
          the casino job robs the <b>Casino vault</b> (its own pot, refilled by casino heist buy-ins) and the bank job cracks <b>Fort Knox</b> (half of everything spent in rooms flows into it). The incentive budget keeps both at 2M or more.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!heist</code> · <code>!join</code> · <code>!bail</code> · <code>!shop</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> heists pay out of the vaults, like a dividend. A failed vault door leaves the loot in the vault. Heists never burn PAT, and the admins can switch the heist faucet on and off.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🗺️</span> Turf Wars</h3>
        <p>Gangs fight over the districts on this season's map (the map changes every season). Each district runs a business
          that earns its owner PAT every day. Claim, raid, defend, and climb the season score.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!turf</code> · <code>!claim</code> · <code>!raid</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> turf income and the season prize are paid from the incentive budget, and a small slice of blackjack, hold'em and fight rake still goes to the gang that owns the matching business. <b>Coming later:</b> room turf wars, where gangs take control of real rooms and their vaults.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🎩</span> Gangs</h3>
        <p>A gang shares a treasury, wages and heat. Take turf together, defend it together, split what it earns.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!gang create [TAG] name</code> · <code>!gang invite @user</code></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 11. Polls -->
  <section id="polls">
    <div class="ds-eyebrow ac">HAVE YOUR SAY</div>
    <h2 class="ds-h2"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🗳️</span> Polls</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <p>Free, no PAT involved. One vote per person, in the room or on the site. Every poll gets a live results page;
          see them all on <a href="/polls">/polls</a>.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!poll Best pizza? pepperoni, margherita, pineapple</code> · type the number to vote · <code>!results</code></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 12. Website -->
  <section id="web">
    <div class="ds-eyebrow ac">FROM ANY BROWSER</div>
    <h2 class="ds-h2"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🌐</span> Doing it all from the website</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <p>Once a chat account is linked to your PATV account (Edit profile → Connections; for Camfrog, type
          <code>!verify</code> with the code in a room), you can do most of this right here:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>create and trade <a href="/markets">markets</a>, join <a href="/wagers">pools and wagers</a></li>
          <li>post, fund and claim <a href="/bounties">bounties</a></li>
          <li>vote in and start <a href="/polls">polls</a></li>
          <li>buy <a href="/lotto">lotto</a> tickets</li>
          <li>manage your stashes and loans on <a href="/wallet">/wallet</a></li>
          <li>watch the vaults and your stakes on <a href="/staking">/staking</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>It's the same balance and the same rules as in the room; Pepe places your orders through the normal checks.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- Fees -->
  <section id="fees">
    <div class="ds-eyebrow ac">AT A GLANCE</div>
    <h2 class="ds-h2"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🧾</span> Fees</h2>
    <p class="lead">Fees aren't burned, and they <a href="#protocol">follow risk</a>: a fee goes to the vault that put up the PAT for the
      activity (Bank, House or Market maker). Fines, the bounty fee and the shop fee go to the Federal Reserve, and spending
      in a room is split between Fort Knox and that pad's vault. <span class="cfg">⚙ = set by the admins, can change.</span></p>
    <div class="ds-tbl">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>WHAT</th><th>FEE</th><th>NOTES</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Wheel spin</td><td class="n">5,000 / spin</td><td>All into the House, which pays the prizes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>+100 Daily Gold Spins</td><td class="n">3M, +1M per copy owned</td><td>Shop item; all into the House</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Blackjack</td><td class="n">losing bets</td><td>To the House; the House pays the winners</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hold'em</td><td class="n">small rake <span class="cfg">⚙</span></td><td>Taken from pots, to the House</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Lotto ticket</td><td class="n">1,000 / ticket</td><td>40% to the Lotto pot (jackpot, max 100M), 60% to the House (pays the fixed prizes)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bingo</td><td class="n">10% of card sales</td><td>House cut; the rest is the prize pool</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1-on-1 wager</td><td class="n">5% of the pot</td><td>Only when someone wins; voids are free. To the House</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Betting pool</td><td class="n">5% of losing side <span class="cfg">⚙</span></td><td>Winners never get back less than they bet. To the Market maker</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Prediction market</td><td class="n">2% per trade</td><td>On every buy and sell, to the Market maker that seeded the market</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bounty</td><td class="n">5% of payout</td><td>Refunds on cancel or expiry are free. To the Federal Reserve</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Fines</td><td class="n">set by staff</td><td>To the Federal Reserve</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Shop listings</td><td class="n">10% of the sale</td><td>The seller gets 90%; the fee goes to the Federal Reserve</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Spending in a room</td><td class="n">the item's price</td><td>Half to Fort Knox, half to that pad's vault (all to Fort Knox in your own pad or with no room)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Reserve loan</td><td class="n">Reserve rate</td><td>Interest and late penalties to the Bank that lent it</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Player loan</td><td class="n">10% of interest</td><td>To the Bank; principal never taxed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Late loan</td><td class="n">+2% / day</td><td>On what's still owed, capped at +50% of the loan</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Duel / Brawl / Arena</td><td class="n">small cut <span class="cfg">⚙</span></td><td>Shared by the Federal Reserve and the Fight Club turf business (to Fort Knox once room turf wars arrive)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Staking yield cap</td><td class="n">above 25% APR <span class="cfg">⚙</span></td><td>Stakers' weekly share above the cap rejoins the rest of the surplus</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Fee splits</td><td class="n"><span class="cfg">⚙</span></td><td>Where each fee goes is set in the routing table</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

